# Files that run on Linux must keep Unix line endings, whatever platform
# checks them out. A CRLF shell script fails on bash with a confusing error
# that names the wrong thing.

lab/scripts/telos-archive text eol=lf
*.sh                      text eol=lf

# EVERY file in lab/configs is pinned by SHA256 in docs/DECISIONS.md. Git must
# never rewrite a single byte of any of them, or the committed file stops
# matching the hash and the claim that the lab runs the committed config
# becomes false. This already happened twice on 2026-09-02, to
# sysmonconfig.xml and then to wazuh-agent-ossec.conf, because
# core.autocrlf is true on the build host.
#
# The rule covers the whole directory on purpose. Naming files one at a time
# is how the second one was missed.
lab/configs/** -text
